1
00:00:46,045 --> 00:00:47,088
Oh, no.

2
00:00:48,297 --> 00:00:49,340
Oh, damn it!

3
00:01:04,272 --> 00:01:06,983
"Get the kids inside!
Let's go!"

4
00:01:08,359 --> 00:01:09,402
Move!

5
00:01:12,113 --> 00:01:13,364
"All right, you know what to do!"

6
00:01:15,575 --> 00:01:16,826
Quickly! Quickly!

7
00:01:20,079 --> 00:01:21,122
"Get 'em inside!"

8
00:01:22,164 --> 00:01:23,583
All right, let's go, men.
This is not a drill.

9
00:01:23,708 --> 00:01:25,751
Take the guns.
Go get your ammo.

10
00:01:26,627 --> 00:01:27,670
That's it.

11
00:01:52,403 --> 00:01:54,655
I'm Special Agent Dennis Abbott
with the FBI.

12
00:01:57,241 --> 00:01:58,284
Means nothing here.

13
00:01:58,826 --> 00:01:59,869
Well, that's okay, son.

14
00:02:00,494 --> 00:02:02,330
I'd like to speak
with whoever's in charge here.

15
00:02:03,080 --> 00:02:05,124
They'll send someone out
if they wanna send someone out.

16
00:02:25,645 --> 00:02:27,021
Easy! Easy.

17
00:02:29,357 --> 00:02:33,110
Guys, does it have to be so serious?
Can we just relax a little?

18
00:03:11,730 --> 00:03:12,773
It's the DOJ again.

19
00:03:13,299 --> 00:03:14,341
{\an8}Need to get used to it.

20
00:03:14,466 --> 00:03:16,552
{\an8}Our victim was a high-profile
U.S. attorney.

21
00:03:16,677 --> 00:03:18,721
{\an8}The solicitor general's
demanding answers.

22
00:03:21,390 --> 00:03:23,017
"Uh, no problemo, Moises."

23
00:03:23,434 --> 00:03:24,768
Uh, they're...
they're with me.

24
00:03:32,568 --> 00:03:33,611
Hey, Jane.

25
00:03:33,944 --> 00:03:35,613
- How was the flight?
- Fine.

26
00:03:35,904 --> 00:03:37,781
{\an8}- How long you been here?
- Oh, about an hour or so.

27
00:03:38,324 --> 00:03:41,785
{\an8}Yeah, that thing is very smooth,
very smooth on the freeway.

28
00:03:42,202 --> 00:03:45,205
I told you it'd be faster to drive.
Where's, uh, Lisbon? No Lisbon?

29
00:03:45,372 --> 00:03:47,583
Back in Austin. She's still dealing
with Ardiles' murder.

30
00:03:51,253 --> 00:03:52,546
- Oh, I'm fine.
- No, thanks.

31
00:03:53,422 --> 00:03:55,049
{\an8}You're missing out.
It's very, very good.

32
00:03:55,591 --> 00:03:56,634
{\an8}Uh, Commander Delgado

33
00:03:56,842 --> 00:03:59,386
{\an8}Special Agent Fischer,
Special Agent Cho.

34
00:04:01,305 --> 00:04:03,557
As soon as I heard the victim was
an attorney for the U.S. Government

35
00:04:03,682 --> 00:04:05,309
I made this case my top priority.

36
00:04:05,976 --> 00:04:07,019
This way, please.

37
00:04:11,273 --> 00:04:13,984
{\an8}So, Commander Delgado, how did you ID
the body so quickly?

38
00:04:14,151 --> 00:04:15,361
{\an8}Medical alert bracelet.

39
00:04:16,320 --> 00:04:17,905
This is Edith Firlock.

40
00:04:18,364 --> 00:04:21,784
53 years of age, had a severe nut
and dairy allergy.

41
00:04:22,284 --> 00:04:24,828
{\an8}That's not what killed her.
It was a bullet to the brain.

42
00:04:25,788 --> 00:04:27,498
{\an8}I've already conducted
my examination.

43
00:04:27,748 --> 00:04:28,791
Thank you, Jane.

44
00:04:29,875 --> 00:04:32,670
- What time was the body found?
- 8:00 this morning.

45
00:04:33,045 --> 00:04:35,381
Lack of blood on-scene suggests
that she was shot somewhere else

46
00:04:35,506 --> 00:04:36,548
and dumped here.

47
00:04:36,715 --> 00:04:39,385
- Any witnesses see the body arrive?
- None that will talk about it.

48
00:04:39,551 --> 00:04:41,762
Clean shot to the back
of the head, execution-style.

49
00:04:42,012 --> 00:04:43,055
Could be Juarez cartel.

50
00:04:43,555 --> 00:04:45,474
The local police are exploring
that angle right now.

51
00:04:45,974 --> 00:04:48,686
{\an8}I'm telling you guys, the commander
and I have been through all of this.

52
00:04:49,061 --> 00:04:50,521
Let's just save a little time,
shall we?

53
00:04:50,813 --> 00:04:51,855
Have a look at the t-shirt.

54
00:04:54,483 --> 00:04:55,526
The sandals.

55
00:04:56,819 --> 00:04:57,861
And this...

56
00:04:58,862 --> 00:04:59,905
tattoo.

57
00:05:00,197 --> 00:05:01,532
It looks like an insignia.

58
00:05:02,908 --> 00:05:05,244
{\an8}So, she has a tattoo
and likes casual clothing.

59
00:05:05,494 --> 00:05:07,746
{\an8}But she doesn't.
She's a federal attorney.

60
00:05:08,455 --> 00:05:11,875
The clear nail polish and the conservative
hairstyle suggest that she...

61
00:05:12,126 --> 00:05:14,878
she worked very hard to look
well-groomed and authoritative...

62
00:05:15,963 --> 00:05:18,966
Yet she's dressed up
as an old-fashioned hippie.

63
00:05:20,676 --> 00:05:22,678
{\an8}It's a costume.
Undercover.

64
00:05:23,595 --> 00:05:24,638
What is that about?

65
00:05:24,972 --> 00:05:28,058
{\an8}Firlock lived in Fort Worth. Do we know
why she was in Mexico?

66
00:05:28,308 --> 00:05:29,977
Nah, she had no official business
down here.

67
00:05:30,269 --> 00:05:33,063
{\an8}Border patrol says Edith Firlock
never crossed into Mexico.

68
00:05:33,439 --> 00:05:35,232
{\an8}We have no record of her
flying or driving here.

69
00:05:35,441 --> 00:05:36,900
{\an8}Well, she crossed
the border somehow.

70
00:05:37,067 --> 00:05:38,777
{\an8}I'll call Wylie, check the surveillance
on our side.

71
00:05:43,824 --> 00:05:44,867
{\an8}So, lunch.

72
00:05:46,452 --> 00:05:47,494
You like tamales?

73
00:05:54,084 --> 00:05:55,127
Ms. Graham?

74
00:05:55,669 --> 00:05:56,712
{\an8}Just call me Elsie.

75
00:05:57,713 --> 00:05:59,298
{\an8}Oh, before I forget...

76
00:06:00,758 --> 00:06:02,593
{\an8}this was Edith's,
they asked me to bring it.

77
00:06:02,885 --> 00:06:04,303
{\an8}Thank you.
Please, take a seat.

78
00:06:07,055 --> 00:06:08,724
{\an8}Edith was always
on that thing.

79
00:06:09,475 --> 00:06:12,019
{\an8}If she wasn't prepping
for a case, she was photo-sharing.

80
00:06:12,644 --> 00:06:14,730
And how long had you been renting
a room from Edith?

81
00:06:15,063 --> 00:06:16,106
Five years.

82
00:06:16,774 --> 00:06:19,693
{\an8}We met when she helped me beat
an intent-to-distribute charge.

83
00:06:20,277 --> 00:06:22,780
{\an8}Never carry a suitcase
across state lines for a man

84
00:06:22,905 --> 00:06:24,198
{\an8}no matter how good he looks.

85
00:06:24,907 --> 00:06:26,492
Can you think of anybody
in Edith's life

86
00:06:26,617 --> 00:06:27,701
who may have had
a problem with her?

87
00:06:27,951 --> 00:06:29,119
{\an8}With Edith? No one.

88
00:06:30,037 --> 00:06:31,580
{\an8}She was the genuine article.

89
00:06:32,664 --> 00:06:35,083
{\an8}A little gruff,
but she saw the good in people.

90
00:06:35,667 --> 00:06:36,919
Certainly saved my life.

91
00:06:37,711 --> 00:06:40,088
{\an8}Uh, you're the last person
we can find who saw her

92
00:06:40,214 --> 00:06:41,548
{\an8}and that was yesterday
at what time?

93
00:06:42,049 --> 00:06:43,091
{\an8}6:00 a.m.

94
00:06:43,675 --> 00:06:46,136
{\an8}I was leaving for the early shift
when I ran into her.

95
00:06:46,845 --> 00:06:48,472
{\an8}Said she'd be back
later that evening.

96
00:06:49,598 --> 00:06:50,641
Now she's dead.

97
00:06:51,934 --> 00:06:53,143
Did she say where she was going?

98
00:06:54,520 --> 00:06:55,562
I didn't ask.

99
00:06:56,188 --> 00:06:58,440
And you're sure she was planning
on coming home last night?

100
00:06:58,941 --> 00:07:00,818
She had a deposition
this morning.

101
00:07:01,610 --> 00:07:03,111
Edith would've never missed that.

102
00:07:04,112 --> 00:07:05,531
Her clients were her life.

103
00:07:07,699 --> 00:07:09,535
If Firlock drove
from Forth Worth to Juarez

104
00:07:09,660 --> 00:07:12,079
she wasn't planning to stay long.
That's a half-day drive each way.

105
00:07:12,371 --> 00:07:13,622
Not to mention the time
she would've spent

106
00:07:13,747 --> 00:07:16,375
- just getting through the border crossing.
- Oh, it's... it's not that bad.

107
00:07:16,792 --> 00:07:18,377
Shorter than airport traffic,
apparently.

108
00:07:18,585 --> 00:07:20,170
I, uh...
I got some lunch.

109
00:07:20,587 --> 00:07:22,673
Tamales de carnitas.

110
00:07:23,882 --> 00:07:25,759
Cho, little napkin, there.

111
00:07:27,344 --> 00:07:28,887
- There we go.
- Thank you.

112
00:07:30,639 --> 00:07:32,474
What if the victim didn't drive
herself to Mexico?

113
00:07:32,933 --> 00:07:35,477
You mean what if she was abducted?
Yeah, that's a possibility.

114
00:07:36,228 --> 00:07:37,271
What do you think, Jane?

115
00:07:37,396 --> 00:07:39,523
Well, I think you're gonna want
some salsa verde with that.

116
00:07:40,399 --> 00:07:41,650
- There you go.
- Thanks.

117
00:07:41,775 --> 00:07:43,235
What do you think
about the case?

118
00:07:44,736 --> 00:07:46,655
Well, she was in costume

119
00:07:46,780 --> 00:07:48,699
pretending to be an old,
leftist hippie.

120
00:07:49,366 --> 00:07:51,910
Uh, you solve that mystery
and I think you'll catch your killer.

121
00:07:52,160 --> 00:07:53,203
If you're right.

122
00:07:54,329 --> 00:07:58,125
Well, it does require paying attention
to some of the details.

123
00:07:59,668 --> 00:08:01,962
Everyone betrays truths
about themselves.

124
00:08:02,504 --> 00:08:04,047
Speaking of which, ah, Cho...

125
00:08:05,465 --> 00:08:07,926
Almost forgot, I got you those
at the marketplace.

126
00:08:17,227 --> 00:08:19,187
- Mexican jumping beans.
- I knew you'd love 'em.

127
00:08:21,607 --> 00:08:23,942
I used to love jumping beans.
Totally forgot about 'em.

128
00:08:25,068 --> 00:08:26,111
How did you know?

129
00:08:26,445 --> 00:08:28,488
Well, knowing what people
secretly want is what I do.

130
00:08:28,947 --> 00:08:31,283
Really?
What do I secretly want?

131
00:08:33,702 --> 00:08:34,870
You sure you want me
to answer that?

132
00:08:35,287 --> 00:08:36,330
Tell me.

133
00:08:37,831 --> 00:08:40,042
Well, how about I do one better?
I'll just get you one.

134
00:08:40,417 --> 00:08:41,501
It'll be my little gift to you.

135
00:08:42,085 --> 00:08:43,128
One what?

136
00:08:45,422 --> 00:08:46,465
Come in!

137
00:08:48,634 --> 00:08:50,427
Commander, thank you very much.

138
00:08:50,552 --> 00:08:52,304
What a great lunch suggestion.
It's delicious.

139
00:08:52,429 --> 00:08:53,472
You want some?

140
00:08:53,597 --> 00:08:57,309
No, no. I'm good. I just came to let
you know that this isn't a cartel hit.

141
00:08:57,601 --> 00:08:58,644
How can you be sure?

142
00:08:58,810 --> 00:09:01,605
The local police tell me that there's a field
very close, very secluded

143
00:09:01,855 --> 00:09:03,899
where the Juarez cartel
put their bodies.

144
00:09:04,274 --> 00:09:05,317
It's a custom.

145
00:09:05,567 --> 00:09:07,069
Everybody around here
uses the field

146
00:09:07,194 --> 00:09:08,236
when they
have a body to dump.

147
00:09:08,528 --> 00:09:09,905
So not a local.

148
00:09:10,072 --> 00:09:11,448
Could be an old client
with a beef

149
00:09:11,698 --> 00:09:13,575
blames his lawyer
for prison time, wants payback.

150
00:09:13,742 --> 00:09:16,495
Yeah. We need to look
at Firlock's case files.

151
00:09:17,037 --> 00:09:19,122
I'll call Abbott.
Meet you back in Austin?

152
00:09:19,748 --> 00:09:20,791
Yeah. I may be a little delayed.

153
00:09:20,916 --> 00:09:22,167
I wanna go take another look
at the crime scene

154
00:09:22,292 --> 00:09:23,377
before I roll outta here.

155
00:09:27,381 --> 00:09:30,050
According to Firlock's colleagues
she had the best record

156
00:09:30,300 --> 00:09:32,511
of any defense attorney
in the Fifth Circuit.

157
00:09:32,970 --> 00:09:35,931
Gave the ASUAs hell
and did it with very little money.

158
00:09:36,056 --> 00:09:37,599
No wonder
she was highly sought after.

159
00:09:38,141 --> 00:09:41,478
But still, being a federal public defender
seems like a thankless job.

160
00:09:41,603 --> 00:09:44,564
And they also said that threats
of violence from her clients

161
00:09:44,856 --> 00:09:45,899
were very common.

162
00:09:46,274 --> 00:09:48,193
These case files just arrived
from Fort Worth.

163
00:09:48,944 --> 00:09:51,029
Fischer and Cho are on their way
to help you dig into 'em.

164
00:09:51,321 --> 00:09:52,364
Looks like fun.

165
00:09:59,579 --> 00:10:01,456
What exactly
are you looking for, Mr. Jane?

166
00:10:03,083 --> 00:10:04,126
Well...

167
00:10:05,085 --> 00:10:06,920
You didn't know
there was a body dump near here

168
00:10:07,045 --> 00:10:08,714
but, you know,
that's to be expected.

169
00:10:09,381 --> 00:10:11,925
You're an important state official.
But the locals knew.

170
00:10:13,010 --> 00:10:15,220
And what better way is there to hide
your involvement in the crime

171
00:10:15,429 --> 00:10:16,596
than to frame a cartel?

172
00:10:17,180 --> 00:10:19,516
- There is no better way.
- Exactly.

173
00:10:20,392 --> 00:10:24,312
So why dump the body here
and not in the body dump?

174
00:10:24,896 --> 00:10:26,732
Must be because
it's more convenient here.

175
00:10:28,066 --> 00:10:29,985
But why is it more convenient?

176
00:11:18,325 --> 00:11:19,367
Mr. Jane.

177
00:11:27,375 --> 00:11:28,418
Mr. Jane!

178
00:11:39,971 --> 00:11:41,014
Mr. Jane?

179
00:11:46,770 --> 00:11:47,813
What have you got, Wylie?

180
00:11:47,938 --> 00:11:49,898
I searched border surveillance
for a 100-mile radius

181
00:11:50,023 --> 00:11:51,191
around the city of Juarez.

182
00:11:51,608 --> 00:11:52,776
And did Firlock's car pass through?

183
00:11:52,901 --> 00:11:55,195
No. Her vehicle didn't clear
any bridges or border crossings

184
00:11:55,320 --> 00:11:56,530
in the past 24 hours.

185
00:11:56,988 --> 00:12:00,033
Okay. Well, if she was abducted,
she might've been in a different vehicle.

186
00:12:00,450 --> 00:12:02,035
It's possible, but not likely.

187
00:12:02,160 --> 00:12:04,663
Well, first of all, her car should've
been found abandoned by now.

188
00:12:04,788 --> 00:12:06,248
We have half of Texas
looking for it.

189
00:12:06,998 --> 00:12:09,584
Then there's the thermal-imaging
scanners at the border.

190
00:12:09,835 --> 00:12:12,337
Even a body in a trunk will have
registered a heat signature

191
00:12:12,462 --> 00:12:14,172
but there were no suspicious
reports last night.

192
00:12:14,923 --> 00:12:16,758
All right. What about illegal routes?

193
00:12:17,134 --> 00:12:19,553
I checked with the DEA
ICE, and border patrol...

194
00:12:19,678 --> 00:12:20,929
No unusual sightings.

195
00:12:21,680 --> 00:12:24,182
It... It... it's like Firlock appeared
in Juarez outta thin air.

196
00:12:29,604 --> 00:12:31,481
- Hey, Jane.
- "I... I think I know how Edith"

197
00:12:31,606 --> 00:12:34,317
"made it to Mexico but I need you
to track my phone."

198
00:12:34,568 --> 00:12:36,319
Uh, just tell me where you are.

199
00:12:36,570 --> 00:12:39,781
"Well, that's the problem.
I don't really know where I am."

200
00:12:40,323 --> 00:12:42,284
Jane, I'm gonna need a little
more information than that.

201
00:12:44,202 --> 00:12:45,245
Jane.

202
00:12:47,581 --> 00:12:49,374
- What's wrong with Jane?
- I don't know.

203
00:12:50,417 --> 00:12:51,459
Jane, are you there?

204
00:13:11,855 --> 00:13:13,440
Well, these are the coordinates
Jane was calling from.

205
00:13:14,983 --> 00:13:16,026
No, this can't be right.

206
00:13:18,403 --> 00:13:19,446
We had to cross the border.

207
00:13:19,571 --> 00:13:21,281
The map says
we're in Gentry, Texas, now.

208
00:13:21,406 --> 00:13:22,449
We left Jane in Mexico.

209
00:13:25,452 --> 00:13:26,870
Well, the Rio Grande's
right down there.

210
00:13:29,497 --> 00:13:30,624
Let me try calling him again.

211
00:13:36,796 --> 00:13:37,881
We got a truck coming
down the road.

212
00:13:47,140 --> 00:13:49,643
What the hell you doing?
This is private property!

213
00:13:51,186 --> 00:13:53,021
FBI, put down the rifle.

214
00:13:54,439 --> 00:13:55,482
Show me your badge.

215
00:13:55,649 --> 00:13:57,442
Can't do that until
you lower your weapon.

216
00:13:58,318 --> 00:14:00,528
I ain't lowering my weapon
until you show me a badge.

217
00:14:03,573 --> 00:14:04,616
"Uh, hey, guys."

218
00:14:05,784 --> 00:14:07,410
"Sorry to interrupt. Um..."

219
00:14:08,078 --> 00:14:13,208
"Just listen. Whatever happens...
whatever happens, don't shoot."

220
00:14:18,713 --> 00:14:19,756
Ah!

221
00:14:24,427 --> 00:14:25,470
Jane?

222
00:14:30,642 --> 00:14:31,893
Jane, where did you come from?

223
00:14:33,353 --> 00:14:34,396
Mexico!

224
00:14:35,230 --> 00:14:36,273
In a tunnel!

225
00:14:42,251 --> 00:14:44,629
"This is the Juarez cartel
we're talking about."

226
00:14:45,088 --> 00:14:47,340
I had no choice
but to let them dig that tunnel!

227
00:14:50,385 --> 00:14:52,303
You let them build
a thousand-yard tunnel into your land

228
00:14:53,054 --> 00:14:54,764
and yet you got nothing
in return, Mr. Phelps?

229
00:14:55,181 --> 00:14:56,224
Of course I did.

230
00:14:56,724 --> 00:14:59,519
But what was I supposed to do?
They threatened my family.

231
00:15:00,144 --> 00:15:01,896
We found blood on your land,
a lot of it...

232
00:15:03,439 --> 00:15:04,941
200 feet
from your tunnel's entrance.

233
00:15:06,734 --> 00:15:09,570
- I don't know anything about that.
- Type B, same as Edith Firlock.

234
00:15:09,904 --> 00:15:12,198
- Who is Edith Firlock?
- The innocent woman you killed

235
00:15:12,407 --> 00:15:14,367
and dragged through the tunnel
and dumped in Juarez.

236
00:15:14,700 --> 00:15:17,286
It's only a matter of time
before we find your DNA on her body.

237
00:15:22,708 --> 00:15:25,420
- That's not how it happened at all.
- No? Tell me.

238
00:15:27,213 --> 00:15:29,465
Early yesterday morning,
I went to check on the cattle

239
00:15:29,799 --> 00:15:30,842
saw some buzzards.

240
00:15:32,760 --> 00:15:34,804
Drove out, thinking that
one of my herd was down.

241
00:15:35,221 --> 00:15:36,264
Found that woman dead.

242
00:15:37,348 --> 00:15:39,976
She was lying there with her arms
crossed, all creepy-like.

243
00:15:42,812 --> 00:15:44,856
Last thing I needed
was cops snooping around.

244
00:15:47,483 --> 00:15:48,526
So I moved her.

245
00:15:49,068 --> 00:15:50,111
What'd you do with her car?

246
00:15:51,237 --> 00:15:52,822
"There was no car.
It was just the body."

247
00:15:53,614 --> 00:15:57,034
Mr. Phelps is guilty of many things
that will put him in jail for a long time.

248
00:15:57,160 --> 00:15:59,203
But you don't think
he killed Firlock.

249
00:15:59,537 --> 00:16:00,580
No, I don't.

250
00:16:01,038 --> 00:16:02,081
Neither do I.

251
00:16:02,665 --> 00:16:03,708
No?

252
00:16:08,796 --> 00:16:10,298
We would've found more blood
in the tunnel.

253
00:16:10,590 --> 00:16:11,632
So we agree.

254
00:16:12,258 --> 00:16:13,509
I won't tell anyone if you don't.

255
00:16:14,260 --> 00:16:16,679
But someone did kill that woman
on Phelps' property.

256
00:16:17,096 --> 00:16:18,514
Someone who didn't know
about the tunnel

257
00:16:18,639 --> 00:16:20,141
or they would've hidden
the body themselves.

258
00:16:20,266 --> 00:16:22,268
What I'm more interested in
is how Phelps found the body.

259
00:16:22,560 --> 00:16:24,145
With her arms crossed.

260
00:16:24,270 --> 00:16:25,813
Well, it suggests a degree
of care.

261
00:16:26,272 --> 00:16:27,607
So you think
the killer knew Firlock.

262
00:16:27,773 --> 00:16:30,860
Oh, great.
Is this what I secretly want?

263
00:16:30,985 --> 00:16:32,487
- Yeah, this better be good.
- Agent Fischer

264
00:16:32,612 --> 00:16:35,323
I... I completed an image search
for that tattoo you sent over.

265
00:16:35,573 --> 00:16:37,950
I'm sorry it took so long.
Firlock's tattoo is an insignia

266
00:16:38,075 --> 00:16:40,369
for a legal defense fund
that closed down 25 years ago.

267
00:16:40,495 --> 00:16:41,662
- She was a member?
- That's right.

268
00:16:41,787 --> 00:16:43,498
They represented fringe groups, uh...

269
00:16:43,623 --> 00:16:45,583
Oh, my God.
Is that a Tamagotchi?

270
00:16:48,044 --> 00:16:50,004
Excuse me.
May I? Thank you.

271
00:16:50,254 --> 00:16:51,297
I... I bought that for you.

272
00:16:52,632 --> 00:16:54,717
I loved these things
so much as a kid!

273
00:16:55,468 --> 00:16:58,513
I... I killed my fair share,
but I'm gonna keep this one alive.

274
00:16:59,347 --> 00:17:00,890
- Thank you so much!
- My pleasure.

275
00:17:04,060 --> 00:17:06,604
Wow. You must've been a real hoot
at other kids' birthday parties.

276
00:17:09,440 --> 00:17:13,110
What was Firlock doing in Gentry?
It's a long way to drive for a day trip.

277
00:17:13,444 --> 00:17:15,238
Mm. But it's a nice drive, though.

278
00:17:16,113 --> 00:17:17,532
How you doing
on the case files?

279
00:17:17,698 --> 00:17:18,741
They put me to sleep.

280
00:17:18,908 --> 00:17:21,118
I decided to take a break
and look at her photo-share site.

281
00:17:21,369 --> 00:17:22,411
Check this out.

282
00:17:24,580 --> 00:17:27,583
These are the pictures she downloaded
the night before she left for Gentry.

283
00:17:28,167 --> 00:17:30,253
- Farmers market. Lovely.
- I wonder where it is.

284
00:17:30,711 --> 00:17:32,421
Well, that's easy...
Gentry.

285
00:17:33,047 --> 00:17:34,173
- How do you know?
- Those wind turbines

286
00:17:34,340 --> 00:17:36,551
are the same ones you can see
from Phelps' ranch.

287
00:17:38,386 --> 00:17:40,263
Okay, so she sees
these photos on the internet

288
00:17:40,429 --> 00:17:43,182
and the next day, she jumps in her car
for an all-day road trip?

289
00:17:43,307 --> 00:17:44,350
Why does somebody do that?

290
00:17:44,475 --> 00:17:46,769
Well, that corn on the cob
looks very tasty.

291
00:17:48,062 --> 00:17:50,523
I could drive my Airstream
down to Gentry.

292
00:17:51,440 --> 00:17:54,026
- Wanna join me?
- In the silver bucket? No, thanks.

293
00:17:54,277 --> 00:17:55,611
Well, Fischer it is, then.

294
00:17:56,153 --> 00:17:58,823
I'm still trying to track down
whoever tapped our cellphones

295
00:17:58,990 --> 00:18:00,199
and killed Ardiles.

296
00:18:00,324 --> 00:18:01,867
Van Pelt's got a lead
but I'm waiting for a judge

297
00:18:01,993 --> 00:18:03,744
to sign off on a warrant
to search the property.

298
00:18:03,953 --> 00:18:06,038
- Well, J.J. owes me a favor.
- Laroche?

299
00:18:06,414 --> 00:18:09,083
Yeah, I heard he's working
Internal Affairs at SFPD.

300
00:18:09,500 --> 00:18:11,460
You snap your fingers,
I bet he'll come running.

301
00:18:11,669 --> 00:18:14,380
We're the last people he'd wanna help.
He lost his job because of us.

302
00:18:14,505 --> 00:18:16,132
Well, I'm not saying
he's gonna wanna help us

303
00:18:16,257 --> 00:18:18,009
but if you just mention
that I'm involved

304
00:18:18,134 --> 00:18:20,511
and that, uh, you know,
he kind of owes me a favor

305
00:18:20,761 --> 00:18:21,846
I think he'd be glad to help.

306
00:18:25,349 --> 00:18:26,392
Just saying.

307
00:18:42,992 --> 00:18:44,035
We're here already?

308
00:18:44,660 --> 00:18:46,579
Yeah, well, we've been on the road
for five hours.

309
00:18:47,371 --> 00:18:48,956
Oh. Guess I dozed.

310
00:18:52,209 --> 00:18:53,252
All right.

311
00:18:53,878 --> 00:18:54,962
Let's go meet the locals.

312
00:18:55,838 --> 00:18:57,673
Here are some photos
of the victim we can show.

313
00:18:58,549 --> 00:18:59,592
Well, it's lunchtime.

314
00:19:00,426 --> 00:19:01,469
There's too many people.

315
00:19:02,345 --> 00:19:04,597
Better to wait till the crowd
thins a bit.

316
00:19:05,348 --> 00:19:07,099
- Where you going?
- I...

317
00:19:08,684 --> 00:19:09,727
am going...

318
00:19:11,354 --> 00:19:13,606
- to take a little nap.
- You're gonna sleep on the job?

319
00:19:22,657 --> 00:19:23,699
Hi, there.

320
00:19:24,075 --> 00:19:25,660
Hi. I was wondering
if you'd seen this woman

321
00:19:25,785 --> 00:19:27,453
anywhere around here
in the past couple of days.

322
00:19:27,745 --> 00:19:29,205
- We're trying to track her down.
- Who are you?

323
00:19:30,414 --> 00:19:31,624
Kim Fischer.
I'm with the FBI.

324
00:19:33,709 --> 00:19:34,752
Yeah, I don't know anything.

325
00:19:37,338 --> 00:19:40,508
I will take that as a "no".
Thank you for your time.

326
00:20:03,030 --> 00:20:04,073
I'll take one of those.

327
00:20:04,490 --> 00:20:06,575
Our peanut butter
is all-natural and hand-ground.

328
00:20:06,867 --> 00:20:07,910
Thank you.

329
00:20:10,496 --> 00:20:11,664
Wow, that's really delicious.

330
00:20:12,498 --> 00:20:14,166
- Clancy.
- Kim.

331
00:20:15,000 --> 00:20:17,503
Clancy, you look like a man who knows
his way around this market.

332
00:20:17,753 --> 00:20:19,255
Well, I've been working here
for a couple of years, so...

333
00:20:19,880 --> 00:20:21,006
I could use your help.

334
00:20:22,591 --> 00:20:23,634
Have you seen this woman?

335
00:20:24,301 --> 00:20:27,096
She might've been here a few days ago
wearing a "Free Mandela" t-shirt.

336
00:20:27,555 --> 00:20:29,306
Oh, yeah.
I remember the t-shirt.

337
00:20:29,432 --> 00:20:30,516
I believe I gave her a sample.

338
00:20:30,891 --> 00:20:33,352
Do you remember anything else?
Uh, did she have anyone with her?

339
00:20:33,936 --> 00:20:36,814
So, are you the cop lady
everybody's talking about?

340
00:20:37,940 --> 00:20:38,983
Cop lady?

341
00:20:39,275 --> 00:20:40,651
Uh, I'm with the FBI.

342
00:20:40,943 --> 00:20:43,446
As an officer of the law, you're required
to announce yourself.

343
00:20:43,571 --> 00:20:45,906
Wow. Okay. Uh, an innocent woman
was murdered.

344
00:20:46,031 --> 00:20:47,616
I'm just looking for information.

345
00:20:47,742 --> 00:20:50,161
Oh, you want the truth, and yet
you approach me with artifice.

346
00:20:50,286 --> 00:20:51,328
What's your name?

347
00:20:52,121 --> 00:20:53,372
Special Agent Fischer.

348
00:20:53,831 --> 00:20:56,584
- Special, indeed.
- Uh, well, Agent Fischer

349
00:20:57,126 --> 00:20:59,044
how do you expect anyone to follow
the rules of the government

350
00:20:59,170 --> 00:21:00,421
if you won't follow them yourself?

351
00:21:09,889 --> 00:21:10,931
Hello, Laroche.

352
00:21:12,600 --> 00:21:13,642
Looks like you're keeping busy.

353
00:21:15,144 --> 00:21:17,229
As keen-eyed as ever,
young Rigsby.

354
00:21:18,230 --> 00:21:19,273
Van Pelt.

355
00:21:19,523 --> 00:21:20,816
Are you enjoying Internal Affairs?

356
00:21:21,233 --> 00:21:25,488
Dealing with mistrust and disdain
for half the paycheck I got at CBI?

357
00:21:26,030 --> 00:21:28,657
No, I am not enjoying
Internal Affairs.

358
00:21:30,117 --> 00:21:32,328
But you're not here to discuss
my problems, are you?

359
00:21:33,412 --> 00:21:35,080
I believe Lisbon called.

360
00:21:37,792 --> 00:21:40,169
Your old team's phones
are being bugged, Ardiles' murder...

361
00:21:40,336 --> 00:21:42,129
Yes, she...
she told me.

362
00:21:44,590 --> 00:21:46,675
To be honest, I am not interested

363
00:21:46,926 --> 00:21:50,471
in the headache
that seems to accompany you all.

364
00:21:51,430 --> 00:21:55,267
As bad as this job is,
it's drama-free.

365
00:21:56,185 --> 00:21:57,228
Good day.

366
00:21:59,480 --> 00:22:01,732
Uh, we were told to remind you
that you owe Jane.

367
00:22:03,275 --> 00:22:05,653
And if you help us out, your debt
with him will be settled.

368
00:22:14,370 --> 00:22:17,665
I will... secure the warrant
and search the premises.

369
00:22:18,833 --> 00:22:20,292
I will let you know
if I find anything.

370
00:22:20,668 --> 00:22:22,169
I would like to assist
with the search.

371
00:22:22,753 --> 00:22:24,922
You're no longer on active duty.

372
00:22:25,089 --> 00:22:26,507
J.J., our lives are at risk here.

373
00:22:27,508 --> 00:22:29,844
Drama... free.

374
00:22:31,929 --> 00:22:32,972
Let's go.

375
00:22:40,938 --> 00:22:41,981
Tough rodeo.

376
00:22:42,773 --> 00:22:44,400
Tough, but not without rewards.

377
00:22:44,942 --> 00:22:47,862
Clancy at the peanut butter stand
remembers giving Firlock a sample.

378
00:22:48,404 --> 00:22:49,864
Oh. Well, that's interesting.

379
00:22:50,406 --> 00:22:52,825
Yeah. Once he heard I was FBI
he shut down like everybody else.

380
00:22:53,951 --> 00:22:56,662
Maybe someone found out Firlock
was a federal PD and took offense.

381
00:22:56,954 --> 00:22:58,330
Well, that's a reasonable theory.

382
00:22:59,456 --> 00:23:00,499
But it's wrong.

383
00:23:04,295 --> 00:23:05,337
Where are you going?

384
00:23:05,713 --> 00:23:08,841
Uh, well, you said that Edith
accepted a peanut butter sample?

385
00:23:11,385 --> 00:23:12,428
Why would she do that?

386
00:23:13,846 --> 00:23:16,515
Her medical alert bracelet
said that she was allergic to nuts.

387
00:23:17,266 --> 00:23:18,642
Bingo. My turn.

388
00:23:21,604 --> 00:23:23,647
Would you care to try some
freshly ground peanut butter?

389
00:23:25,024 --> 00:23:26,066
Oh, yeah.

390
00:23:26,400 --> 00:23:27,443
Don't mind if I do.

391
00:23:34,033 --> 00:23:36,702
- That is delicious. You make that?
- Sure did.

392
00:23:40,247 --> 00:23:42,958
Let me get a jar of that
for the road.

393
00:23:43,208 --> 00:23:45,127
Thanks, and, um...

394
00:23:46,086 --> 00:23:49,340
- And this, one of those. Thank you.
- Mm, how's 10 for both?

395
00:23:50,674 --> 00:23:51,717
Very reasonable.

396
00:23:52,259 --> 00:23:53,302
Where you headed?

397
00:23:54,428 --> 00:23:55,471
Uh, probably west.

398
00:23:56,055 --> 00:23:57,306
Yeah, no...
no set plan

399
00:23:57,431 --> 00:23:59,892
just looking for some level road
to set the silver sovereign on.

400
00:24:00,184 --> 00:24:02,144
- It's a nice rig.
- Yeah, it's home.

401
00:24:02,645 --> 00:24:04,396
At least till I find someplace
to settle down.

402
00:24:05,522 --> 00:24:06,941
Gonna get myself a farm
one day.

403
00:24:07,691 --> 00:24:08,734
It's a good life.

404
00:24:08,984 --> 00:24:10,277
"Gadsden Grove."

405
00:24:10,903 --> 00:24:12,196
"Citizens farm."

406
00:24:12,571 --> 00:24:14,782
- What's the deal with that, huh?
- Just homesteaders

407
00:24:15,199 --> 00:24:16,533
focusing on living our own way.

408
00:24:16,742 --> 00:24:18,160
Oh, yeah. Like...
like a commune?

409
00:24:18,827 --> 00:24:20,955
Nah, none of that hippie stuff.

410
00:24:21,246 --> 00:24:23,582
No, we're just steering clear
of the power grab going on out there.

411
00:24:24,208 --> 00:24:25,250
I feel you.

412
00:24:25,501 --> 00:24:27,378
If a man wants justice
and freedom in this world

413
00:24:27,503 --> 00:24:28,587
he's gotta get it himself.

414
00:24:28,921 --> 00:24:30,047
- That's right.
- Yeah.

415
00:24:31,548 --> 00:24:32,591
Well, nice talking to you.

416
00:24:33,175 --> 00:24:35,177
- Thank you. Better hit the road.
- Yeah.

417
00:24:35,594 --> 00:24:36,637
Hey, you know, if, uh...

418
00:24:37,221 --> 00:24:38,806
if it's farming you like,
you should come visit us.

419
00:24:39,390 --> 00:24:40,432
Take a look-see.

420
00:24:41,600 --> 00:24:43,644
- Well, I don't wanna be any trouble.
- No trouble.

421
00:24:44,478 --> 00:24:45,813
Actually, I'm heading back there
right now.

422
00:24:50,526 --> 00:24:53,153
Yeah, sure, why not?
That's a very generous offer.

423
00:24:53,362 --> 00:24:54,405
- Patrick.
- Alex.

424
00:24:54,780 --> 00:24:56,365
- It's a pleasure to make your acquaintance.
- You, too.

425
00:24:57,533 --> 00:24:59,410
We got a report
on an abandoned vehicle

426
00:24:59,535 --> 00:25:01,662
that matches the description
of Edith Firlock's car.

427
00:25:02,079 --> 00:25:03,122
Really? Where is it?

428
00:25:03,664 --> 00:25:05,833
"Ditched in a gully not far
from your current location."

429
00:25:07,543 --> 00:25:09,420
Great. I'll drive over there with Jane
and we'll check it out.

430
00:25:13,215 --> 00:25:14,258
Hey!

431
00:25:14,800 --> 00:25:16,719
Hey, Jane! Jane!

432
00:25:23,890 --> 00:25:25,851
"Yes, sir.
Sitting on 1,000 acres."

433
00:25:26,226 --> 00:25:29,855
Plenty of space for crops, gardens
private living quarters.

434
00:25:30,647 --> 00:25:32,941
- It's a sweet setup.
- Yep. It's home.

435
00:25:34,735 --> 00:25:36,820
Fully licensed under
the state's concealed-carry laws.

436
00:25:37,612 --> 00:25:39,573
Most of us on the farm here
choose to exercise

437
00:25:39,823 --> 00:25:40,991
our second-amendment rights.

438
00:25:41,450 --> 00:25:42,576
Well, if you like it, I love it.

439
00:25:44,995 --> 00:25:46,038
How'd you end up here?

440
00:25:46,580 --> 00:25:48,331
Well, like you, I looked
to the government for answers

441
00:25:48,498 --> 00:25:49,583
after I got discharged...

442
00:25:50,751 --> 00:25:51,793
only it didn't show up.

443
00:25:52,544 --> 00:25:54,379
So I turned to the bottle
for support.

444
00:25:56,048 --> 00:25:57,090
Well... I've been there.

445
00:25:57,758 --> 00:26:00,927
Lucky for me, the farmer that owned
this place saw my struggle

446
00:26:01,136 --> 00:26:03,346
and helped me
turn my life around.

447
00:26:03,638 --> 00:26:05,599
When he died, he left me all this.

448
00:26:06,683 --> 00:26:08,727
So I decided to do for others
what he did for me...

449
00:26:09,561 --> 00:26:11,813
Help people
find a place to be free.

450
00:26:12,397 --> 00:26:13,440
That's very impressive.

451
00:26:14,191 --> 00:26:15,400
We're always open to good people.

452
00:26:16,276 --> 00:26:17,319
Oh, I don't know.

453
00:26:18,320 --> 00:26:19,613
Can't stay on the road forever, Patrick.

454
00:26:20,572 --> 00:26:21,740
Gotta let it take you someplace.

455
00:26:23,867 --> 00:26:26,244
Stay the night.
Think about it, huh?

456
00:26:33,752 --> 00:26:35,253
Jane, where were you all night?

457
00:26:35,504 --> 00:26:36,546
"I, um..."

458
00:26:36,797 --> 00:26:38,048
I slept at the compound.

459
00:26:38,757 --> 00:26:39,925
With the peanut-butter people?

460
00:26:40,592 --> 00:26:42,177
"Yeah. They're really very nice."

461
00:26:42,302 --> 00:26:46,181
Very nice. And...
and the air here is so clean.

462
00:26:46,723 --> 00:26:47,933
I slept like a baby.

463
00:26:48,809 --> 00:26:49,851
Are you ever coming back?

464
00:26:50,852 --> 00:26:53,688
Yeah, well, as soon as I figure out
who killed Edith Firlock.

465
00:26:54,356 --> 00:26:55,732
What makes you think
the killer's there?

466
00:26:56,358 --> 00:26:58,026
"Well, she drove down to Gentry"

467
00:26:58,151 --> 00:27:00,153
to get in touch with someone
from the peanut farm.

468
00:27:00,278 --> 00:27:02,364
I mean, why else
would she dress like a rebel

469
00:27:02,489 --> 00:27:04,282
and accept a food sample

470
00:27:04,407 --> 00:27:06,535
that could possibly send her
into anaphylactic shock?

471
00:27:06,660 --> 00:27:09,579
- Do you have any leads?
- No, but I have a plan.

472
00:27:10,747 --> 00:27:12,040
"Daylight's a-burning, pilgrim."

473
00:27:12,374 --> 00:27:13,875
Oh, uh, I'll be right out!

474
00:27:14,709 --> 00:27:18,839
Um, I'm gonna need,
uh, a black helicopter and...

475
00:27:19,673 --> 00:27:20,715
a tank.

476
00:27:21,466 --> 00:27:22,509
Ha. Yeah, right.

477
00:27:24,094 --> 00:27:25,137
I'm serious.

478
00:27:25,887 --> 00:27:27,556
- What?
- I'm serious!

479
00:27:27,806 --> 00:27:29,099
I know what we signed up for.

480
00:27:29,474 --> 00:27:30,976
I... I know that we have to support him

481
00:27:31,268 --> 00:27:32,477
and take a back seat to his whims

482
00:27:32,602 --> 00:27:35,188
but he abandoned me
at the farmers market yesterday.

483
00:27:35,564 --> 00:27:37,941
Okay, well, l... let's just think
about this for a second.

484
00:27:40,068 --> 00:27:42,112
Jane is making
a sincere effort to fit in.

485
00:27:42,988 --> 00:27:44,072
No, he's not.

486
00:27:47,492 --> 00:27:49,786
Look at what he gave me
yesterday, huh?

487
00:27:50,704 --> 00:27:53,290
- A robot.
- N-no, no, this is just not a robot.

488
00:27:53,456 --> 00:27:56,459
This is Voltron, okay?
I used to love this when I was a kid.

489
00:27:56,793 --> 00:27:59,379
Dennis... he ditched me.

490
00:28:01,715 --> 00:28:03,049
Okay. Yeah.

491
00:28:05,093 --> 00:28:06,136
Well, that's not cool.

492
00:28:06,261 --> 00:28:09,055
No! No, that is far,
far from cool.

493
00:28:10,056 --> 00:28:12,267
Okay, did Jane have something
to say about it afterwards?

494
00:28:12,392 --> 00:28:15,520
Uh, who knows! He hasn't responded
to my texts or my phone calls ever since.

495
00:28:15,645 --> 00:28:17,480
I... look,
where do we draw the line?

496
00:28:18,064 --> 00:28:19,524
How far do we bend for this man?

497
00:28:21,484 --> 00:28:22,736
I just got off the phone with Jane.

498
00:28:22,861 --> 00:28:25,197
He says he needs a black helicopter,
a convoy of vans

499
00:28:25,322 --> 00:28:27,115
and whatever you have
that looks most like a tank.

500
00:28:31,286 --> 00:28:32,329
Uh, uh, Fischer...

501
00:28:35,165 --> 00:28:36,208
What's her problem?

502
00:28:36,708 --> 00:28:37,751
She'll be fine.

503
00:28:38,877 --> 00:28:40,295
What in the hell
were you just talking about?

504
00:28:46,134 --> 00:28:47,177
Pretty handy with that hammer.

505
00:28:47,761 --> 00:28:49,888
Oh, I've used one
a time or two in my life.

506
00:28:50,722 --> 00:28:51,765
Where'd you grow up?

507
00:28:54,351 --> 00:28:55,393
What's wrong, Patrick?

508
00:28:57,187 --> 00:28:59,981
That helicopter...
it's circling us.

509
00:29:00,523 --> 00:29:03,610
- Must be some border issue.
- No. It's unmarked.

510
00:29:04,194 --> 00:29:05,237
Dark-colored.

511
00:29:05,695 --> 00:29:06,988
Are you thinking what I'm thinking?

512
00:29:07,906 --> 00:29:09,449
Somebody doesn't want us
to know who they are.

513
00:29:12,994 --> 00:29:14,037
What was that about?

514
00:29:14,788 --> 00:29:17,415
Well, I don't wanna freak anyone out
but this is usually how it starts.

515
00:29:18,124 --> 00:29:20,543
They scope the property out
right before they, uh...

516
00:29:20,752 --> 00:29:21,795
Before what?

517
00:29:22,587 --> 00:29:25,423
That FBI agent yesterday,
the one Marcia got a picture of.

518
00:29:25,840 --> 00:29:28,218
You know, she was trying to question us
about this missing woman.

519
00:29:29,636 --> 00:29:31,763
- Feds must think we took her.
- Or killed her.

520
00:29:34,224 --> 00:29:35,267
This will not do.

521
00:29:36,184 --> 00:29:38,645
We're good people.
This is sovereign land.

522
00:29:43,608 --> 00:29:45,193
Guys are a little paranoid,
aren't you?

523
00:29:45,485 --> 00:29:46,987
It's not Waco.
It was one helicopter.

524
00:29:47,237 --> 00:29:49,406
One black helicopter...
never a good sign...

525
00:29:50,115 --> 00:29:52,742
- Unless, of course, you're lost.
- Yeah, better safe than sorry.

526
00:29:53,743 --> 00:29:54,953
We should be preparing ourselves.

527
00:29:55,578 --> 00:29:56,621
Prepare ourselves for what?

528
00:29:57,080 --> 00:29:58,790
A black helicopter
was surveilling the property

529
00:29:58,915 --> 00:29:59,958
not 10 minutes ago.

530
00:30:00,250 --> 00:30:01,960
- A raid?
- Maybe.

531
00:30:07,924 --> 00:30:09,384
Bobby, Katie, let's go!

532
00:30:11,761 --> 00:30:12,804
"Come on, let's go!"

533
00:30:14,139 --> 00:30:16,516
There's, like, a convoy of government
vehicles headed our way.

534
00:30:16,683 --> 00:30:17,934
- How many?
- A lot.

535
00:30:18,310 --> 00:30:20,145
- Oh, my God.
- I'll open the gun locker.

536
00:30:20,729 --> 00:30:22,772
Whoa, now.
We need guns? Really?

537
00:30:23,106 --> 00:30:24,858
It's just a helicopter, a few vans.

538
00:30:36,870 --> 00:30:37,912
Easy, fellas.

539
00:30:39,831 --> 00:30:42,167
Guys, does it have to be
so serious?

540
00:30:42,292 --> 00:30:43,418
Can we just relax a little?

541
00:30:45,086 --> 00:30:46,129
Guns down, people.

542
00:30:47,547 --> 00:30:48,590
Go ahead. Guns down.

543
00:30:50,091 --> 00:30:51,843
All right, everybody.
Lower your weapons.

544
00:30:53,470 --> 00:30:54,512
That's better.

545
00:30:55,722 --> 00:30:58,808
We came here to talk.
No gunplay, please.

546
00:30:59,434 --> 00:31:02,228
My name's Alex Mildray.
I speak for Gadsden Grove.

547
00:31:02,937 --> 00:31:05,273
Mr. Mildray, we have a warrant
to search these premises.

548
00:31:05,690 --> 00:31:06,733
Search it for what?

549
00:31:06,941 --> 00:31:09,569
Evidence pertaining to the abduction
and murder of Edith Firlock.

550
00:31:10,111 --> 00:31:12,238
- Never heard of her.
- Well, that may be.

551
00:31:13,073 --> 00:31:14,991
But somebody on this farm
has heard of her.

552
00:31:16,493 --> 00:31:18,078
Look, we're coming in, sir

553
00:31:19,037 --> 00:31:21,414
and I'd like to have your cooperation
before we do that.

554
00:31:27,379 --> 00:31:30,256
You and I have the power
to save lives right now...

555
00:31:31,758 --> 00:31:32,801
if we can work this out.

556
00:31:39,641 --> 00:31:41,267
I speak for the farm,
but I don't decide.

557
00:31:42,477 --> 00:31:43,520
We gotta put it to a vote.

558
00:31:45,647 --> 00:31:46,689
Okay.

559
00:31:47,482 --> 00:31:50,276
I give you an hour to persuade
your people to stand down.

560
00:31:51,111 --> 00:31:52,153
Then we're coming in...

561
00:31:52,862 --> 00:31:54,280
whether you voted for it or not.

562
00:31:54,697 --> 00:31:55,740
"What do we wanna do, people?"

563
00:31:56,282 --> 00:31:57,575
Do we wanna let
the feds in here?

564
00:31:57,992 --> 00:31:59,035
No!

565
00:31:59,160 --> 00:32:00,787
They say there's a murder suspect
among us.

566
00:32:00,995 --> 00:32:02,330
How do we even know that's true?

567
00:32:02,664 --> 00:32:04,707
We can't let the government
roll all over us.

568
00:32:04,833 --> 00:32:06,751
Right!
They done that all our lives.

569
00:32:06,876 --> 00:32:07,919
- Alex.
- Isn't that why we came here?

570
00:32:08,336 --> 00:32:10,422
I like what you're doing here,
and I wanna help you.

571
00:32:10,797 --> 00:32:12,090
Will you let me speak to them now?

572
00:32:12,590 --> 00:32:14,509
I'm gonna say something
that may shock you

573
00:32:14,759 --> 00:32:15,844
but if you work with me

574
00:32:15,969 --> 00:32:18,221
I guarantee you will come out
of this a big hero.

575
00:32:19,097 --> 00:32:20,140
You will be golden.

576
00:32:20,974 --> 00:32:22,559
I promise.
Yes?

577
00:32:23,601 --> 00:32:24,644
Yeah.

578
00:32:25,979 --> 00:32:28,815
Okay, people.
Fellow citizens, my name is Patrick.

579
00:32:29,441 --> 00:32:30,567
I'm not just a citizen

580
00:32:30,692 --> 00:32:35,113
I'm also a sort of indentured servant
to the FBI out there.

581
00:32:35,947 --> 00:32:38,950
- You're FBI?
- I'm with them, not of them.

582
00:32:39,784 --> 00:32:40,827
Let him speak.

583
00:32:41,995 --> 00:32:43,037
It's the truth.

584
00:32:43,955 --> 00:32:45,248
There's a killer amongst you...

585
00:32:45,874 --> 00:32:48,334
Murdered a good woman
by the name of Edith Firlock.

586
00:32:49,127 --> 00:32:51,212
You know, I can find this
bloodthirsty killer right now

587
00:32:51,337 --> 00:32:52,464
and I can take him out of here

588
00:32:52,589 --> 00:32:55,550
and I can do it
without letting those accursed feds

589
00:32:55,717 --> 00:32:57,719
cross your property line.
How does that sound?

590
00:32:58,595 --> 00:32:59,637
Keep talking.

591
00:32:59,888 --> 00:33:02,474
Edith Firlock drove down to Gentry

592
00:33:02,599 --> 00:33:06,561
to, uh, catch up with someone
from her distant past...

593
00:33:06,686 --> 00:33:09,939
A past where she was
a leftist lawyer.

594
00:33:11,357 --> 00:33:12,817
So anyone under the age of 45

595
00:33:12,942 --> 00:33:15,278
please go to the back
of the barn right now.

596
00:33:15,445 --> 00:33:18,198
Under the age of 45...
back of the barn.

597
00:33:18,323 --> 00:33:19,365
The rest of you, please...

598
00:33:20,283 --> 00:33:21,326
Stay here.

599
00:33:22,494 --> 00:33:24,287
Now, my guess
as to what happened here...

600
00:33:24,662 --> 00:33:28,374
Edith Firlock knew a lot
of radical fringe types

601
00:33:28,500 --> 00:33:29,667
from the old days.

602
00:33:31,544 --> 00:33:32,921
One of those old friends...

603
00:33:34,547 --> 00:33:35,590
is on the run

604
00:33:38,009 --> 00:33:41,054
and using your farm to hide out.

605
00:33:42,639 --> 00:33:45,808
Now, I think
Edith figured that out

606
00:33:45,934 --> 00:33:47,477
and came down
to pay a visit.

607
00:33:50,813 --> 00:33:51,856
Any takers?

608
00:33:56,653 --> 00:33:58,363
The killer also owns their own gun.

609
00:34:00,907 --> 00:34:03,201
Who here doesn't own a firearm?

610
00:34:05,036 --> 00:34:07,413
To the back of the barn, please.
Now we're getting close.

611
00:34:09,332 --> 00:34:10,833
The killer's starting
to get nervous.

612
00:34:15,463 --> 00:34:18,883
The killer feels like
it's 110 degrees in here.

613
00:34:21,511 --> 00:34:24,389
The killer's starting
to feel faint, it's so hot.

614
00:34:27,517 --> 00:34:30,186
Which is not you or you.

615
00:34:32,689 --> 00:34:34,399
Now we're getting very,
very close.

616
00:34:35,775 --> 00:34:39,362
And I would suggest
that the killer can now see Edith...

617
00:34:40,697 --> 00:34:42,198
every time they blink.

618
00:34:44,867 --> 00:34:46,160
Yeah. You can see her, right?

619
00:34:47,495 --> 00:34:48,955
Coming for revenge.

620
00:34:50,540 --> 00:34:52,333
Right in the corner of your vision.

621
00:34:54,794 --> 00:34:56,129
That poor woman.

622
00:35:01,509 --> 00:35:02,552
Oh, stop it!

623
00:35:04,137 --> 00:35:07,181
Marcia, right?
What's your real name, huh?

624
00:35:07,515 --> 00:35:08,558
This is a lie!

625
00:35:08,808 --> 00:35:10,935
Remember who he is!
He's a fed!

626
00:35:11,519 --> 00:35:13,146
- He's the enemy!
- Marcia...

627
00:35:15,356 --> 00:35:16,399
Marcia!

628
00:35:17,442 --> 00:35:18,484
Marcia!

629
00:35:19,652 --> 00:35:20,695
You don't wanna do this.

630
00:35:21,070 --> 00:35:22,488
Don't tell me what I want!

631
00:35:22,822 --> 00:35:25,283
I am so sick of you
telling everybody what they want

632
00:35:25,450 --> 00:35:26,826
what to do, how to think!

633
00:35:28,286 --> 00:35:29,329
Marcia...

634
00:35:31,122 --> 00:35:32,165
it's over.

635
00:35:49,597 --> 00:35:52,558
I ran your fingerprints and they tell
an interesting story, Marcia.

636
00:35:56,354 --> 00:35:57,396
Or...

637
00:35:57,938 --> 00:35:59,315
perhaps I should say...

638
00:36:00,149 --> 00:36:01,192
Rachel.

639
00:36:02,902 --> 00:36:06,238
In 1986, you were implicated
in an eco-terrorism bombing

640
00:36:06,572 --> 00:36:08,115
just south
of the Canadian border.

641
00:36:08,866 --> 00:36:10,284
You call it "terrorism".

642
00:36:11,202 --> 00:36:12,787
We called it "liberating nature."

643
00:36:13,329 --> 00:36:15,373
Edith Firlock's defense fund
represented you

644
00:36:15,539 --> 00:36:16,582
until you skipped bail.

645
00:36:18,793 --> 00:36:21,545
You know, 27 years
is a long time to be on the run.

646
00:36:22,171 --> 00:36:25,549
Oh, it's not so bad
once you get past the first 10 years.

647
00:36:29,136 --> 00:36:30,930
Until the past
shows up on your doorstep.

648
00:36:34,141 --> 00:36:36,977
She said she saw my picture
on some travel blog

649
00:36:37,395 --> 00:36:39,980
that she recognized me instantly.

650
00:36:41,899 --> 00:36:42,942
"Rachel Solket..."

651
00:36:46,028 --> 00:36:47,196
"I believe we need to talk."

652
00:36:48,364 --> 00:36:51,325
"She told me
that if she found me"

653
00:36:51,742 --> 00:36:54,120
"it was only a matter of time
before the authorities did."

654
00:36:54,870 --> 00:36:56,330
"So Firlock showed up
to help you."

655
00:36:56,789 --> 00:36:59,041
"Yeah...
help me turn myself in."

656
00:37:00,876 --> 00:37:03,462
But you had no intention
of turning yourself in.

657
00:37:05,589 --> 00:37:07,007
None whatsoever.

658
00:37:11,429 --> 00:37:13,347
So you shot her at Phelps' ranch

659
00:37:13,681 --> 00:37:15,391
and then you went back
to the market.

660
00:37:18,602 --> 00:37:20,813
She should've left
well enough alone.

661
00:37:23,107 --> 00:37:24,150
Yeah.

662
00:37:24,817 --> 00:37:26,068
It was all her fault.

663
00:37:46,338 --> 00:37:48,215
Hey, Laroche.
Do you have news?

664
00:37:48,591 --> 00:37:49,633
I got the warrant.

665
00:37:49,925 --> 00:37:52,136
I have a physical address
in Sacramento.

666
00:37:52,303 --> 00:37:54,305
- Heading there now.
- That's great. Where is it?

667
00:37:55,264 --> 00:37:56,807
Looks like
it's in the warehouse district.

668
00:37:57,391 --> 00:37:58,851
Okay. Send me the address.
I'll join you.

669
00:37:59,310 --> 00:38:01,896
Do you remember nothing
from our conversation?

670
00:38:02,855 --> 00:38:04,064
Yeah, but I can help you.

671
00:38:04,440 --> 00:38:08,319
I will search and let you know
if I find anything worth your time.

672
00:38:08,778 --> 00:38:10,529
- Listen, Laroche, I...
- Goodbye, Rigsby.

673
00:38:14,492 --> 00:38:16,243
- Hey, honey, you catch that?
- Yeah.

674
00:38:17,828 --> 00:38:20,706
Looks like he's headed
towards Elk Grove.

675
00:38:21,040 --> 00:38:22,958
I'll text you the address
once his car stops.

676
00:38:23,709 --> 00:38:24,752
Thanks.

677
00:38:25,044 --> 00:38:27,087
Uh, Wayne... be careful.

678
00:38:27,922 --> 00:38:29,006
- I love you.
- "Love you."

679
00:38:38,307 --> 00:38:39,350
Hi.

680
00:38:40,726 --> 00:38:41,769
What do you want?

681
00:38:42,144 --> 00:38:45,147
Oh, just wanted to apologize for leaving
you out there without a ride.

682
00:38:45,606 --> 00:38:46,649
I understand.

683
00:38:46,899 --> 00:38:48,609
- All in the line of duty.
- Yeah.

684
00:38:53,697 --> 00:38:54,740
I got you that thing you wanted.

685
00:39:05,376 --> 00:39:06,877
Oh, my God.
How did you...

686
00:39:09,255 --> 00:39:10,297
Where'd you get that?

687
00:39:11,382 --> 00:39:12,508
Jane gave it to me.

688
00:39:13,342 --> 00:39:14,760
Jane gave you a wand?

689
00:39:17,096 --> 00:39:18,264
When I was a girl

690
00:39:18,514 --> 00:39:21,600
I thought I could change so many things
if I just had one of these.

691
00:39:22,393 --> 00:39:23,644
Change what kinda things?

692
00:39:25,145 --> 00:39:27,606
Oh, you know, uh,
make myself invisible

693
00:39:28,232 --> 00:39:30,317
transport myself
to magical places.

694
00:39:31,235 --> 00:39:33,320
You must've been disappointed
when it didn't work.

695
00:39:34,113 --> 00:39:35,155
I never got one.

696
00:39:36,448 --> 00:39:39,076
My mom thought all that princess stuff
was stupid nonsense.

697
00:39:41,328 --> 00:39:42,371
She was right, of course.

698
00:39:44,540 --> 00:39:45,583
Of course.

699
00:40:35,174 --> 00:40:38,302
If you former CBI people
are one thing, it's predictable.

700
00:40:38,719 --> 00:40:39,762
I can explain.

701
00:40:40,095 --> 00:40:43,307
I need to search the premises alone.
You stay outside.

702
00:40:48,854 --> 00:40:49,897
Police!

703
00:40:57,780 --> 00:40:58,822
Police!

704
00:40:59,531 --> 00:41:00,574
Search warrant!

705
00:41:06,997 --> 00:41:08,040
"Rigsby!"

706
00:41:12,127 --> 00:41:15,005
- Everything okay?
- No. It's not okay.

707
00:41:15,214 --> 00:41:16,340
This place is creepy.

708
00:41:16,590 --> 00:41:18,592
If you think I'm gonna search
this dump by myself

709
00:41:18,717 --> 00:41:20,177
you are gravely mistaken.

710
00:41:35,818 --> 00:41:36,860
Do you hear that?

711
00:41:37,611 --> 00:41:39,863
Yeah. It sounded like
a man talking.

712
00:41:57,881 --> 00:41:58,924
J.J.!

713
00:42:08,892 --> 00:42:10,477
My... dog.

714
00:42:11,061 --> 00:42:12,104
It's okay.

715
00:42:12,563 --> 00:42:14,773
It's okay. Just...
Just stay with me.

716
00:42:15,065 --> 00:42:16,775
Just s-stay...
stay with me.

717
00:42:17,484 --> 00:42:18,527
It's okay.

718
00:42:22,906 --> 00:42:23,949
It's okay.


